<title>BELGIUM: Belgian car registrations down 6.2% in yr to May.</title>
<headline>Belgian car registrations down 6.2% in yr to May.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian new car registrations fell 6.2 percent in the year to May compared with the same year-ago period, figures from Belgian Car Federation FEBIAC showed.</p>
<p>Registrations were down 10.9 percent in May 1997 from May 1996.</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CAR REGISTRATIONS May 97	  May 96</p>
<p>    Month			    32,868	  36,881</p>
<p>    Cumulative Jan-May	  196,557	 209,499</p>
<p>May registrations by manufacturer and market share for those above three percent versus 1996 period.</p>
<p> VW	 6,829 (20.8 pct)  vs   7,600  (20.6 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot  4,488 (13.7 pct)  vs   4,505  (12.2 pct)</p>
<p> GM	 3,744 (11.4 pct)  vs   3,910  (10.6 pct)</p>
<p> Renault  3,688 (11.2 pct)  vs   4,430  (12.0 pct)</p>
<p> Ford Mtr 3,272 (10.0 pct)  vs   3,484   (9.4 pct)</p>
<p> BMW	1,679  (5.1 pct)  vs   2,462   (6.7 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat     1,483  (4.5 pct)  vs   1,874   (5.1 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota   1,247  (3.8 pct)  vs   1,668   (4.5 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan   1,184  (3.6 pct)  vs     825   (2.2 pct)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
